# Project Workflow

## Scope discipline

- Change only what the task needs; no drive-by refactors
- If a change would touch **more than one file**, confirm with the user first (unless they already approved the plan)
- Prefer small vertical slices over big rewrites

## Scene & asset ownership

- The agent **edits Unity scenes and prefabs directly** (`.unity`, `.prefab`, YAML) when a feature needs scene wiring — do not leave “assign in Inspector yourself” as the default
- Prefer setups that **work without fragile Inspector-only refs** when possible (e.g. code-built input bindings); still wire required scene refs (SO configs, transforms, components)
- Wire references, components, layers, and default SO links in the scene/prefab as part of the task
- Prefer editing existing scene objects over inventing parallel setup docs
- Be careful with YAML merges; keep scene diffs minimal and intentional
- After scene/prefab edits, briefly tell the user what was wired so they can verify in Editor
- If Play Mode shows missing refs / input errors, fix them yourself in scene/scripts — do not ask the user to drag references

## Structure for scale (MVP-friendly)

Keep folders by **domain**, not by dump:

```
Assets/Scripts/
  Player/
  Weapons/
  Camera/
  UI/
  Core/          # shared primitives, interfaces
  Debug/         # cheats, overlays (keep out of production paths)
Assets/Data/     # ScriptableObject assets (configs, balancing)
```

- One public type per file when practical; filename matches type name
- New feature = new folder/module with a clear boundary
- Shared code lives in `Core/` only if used by 2+ domains
- Game-design tunables live in **ScriptableObjects** under `Assets/Data/`, not as magic numbers in scripts

## Readability checklist before finishing

- Public API of a class is understandable from signatures alone
- Dependencies are explicit (serialized fields, SO configs, clear references)
- Required scene/prefab wiring for the feature is done, not deferred
- No dead code, unused usings, or commented-out blocks left behind
- Errors fail loudly in editor/dev builds; never swallow exceptions silently

## Communication

- Chat with the user in **Russian**
- Identifiers, code, and commit messages in **English**
- Comments in code in **Russian**
- Prefer short, direct answers; expand only when asked
